  "slug": "telomere-genome-63e9",
  "summary": "Annotated genome and metagenome resources now cover bacterial, arthropod and annelid hosts alongside long-read 16S symbiont workflows.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these items is curated, reusable reference infrastructure that links genomes, metagenomes and taxonomy to host or environmental context. BacMap 3.0 integrates annotated bacterial and archaeal genomes across a large species set. ArthroVerse catalogues non-redundant protein families from arthropod-associated metagenomes, annotated with taxonomy and host associations. AnnelidaDB combines genomes, transcriptomes, proteomes, epigenomes, single-cell data and symbiont genomes for annelid species. CAnDi provides a global catalogue of anaerobic digestion microbiomes. These items are dominated by database and knowledgebase design rather than mechanistic tests. The one methods-oriented item, SYMBIO-SCAN, offers a full-length 16S rRNA long-read workflow for bacterial symbiont detection in beetles, validated on a mock community. Its contribution is methodological, resolving symbiont composition from long reads, while the wider set provides standardized resources for comparative analysis across hosts and environments.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
